You need to fix 3 code quality issues in `frontend/src/contexts/AgentContext.tsx`.

Work from: `/Users/cyyeh/Desktop/duckdb-data-agent/.claude/worktrees/implement-memory`

Read the file first, then make these 3 fixes:

## Fix 1: Change `flushTextForStream` signature to accept `string | null`

The `conversationId` parameter should be `string | null` instead of `string`, because `convId` can be null (the "new chat before conversation is created" path). This makes the null-equality comparison `activeConversationIdRef.current === conversationId` intentional rather than accidental via `!` assertion.

Change the signature from:
```typescript
const flushTextForStream = useCallback((state: StreamState, conversationId: string) => {
```
To:
```typescript
const flushTextForStream = useCallback((state: StreamState, conversationId: string | null) => {
```

Then in `sendMessage` and `editMessage`, change all `flushTextForStream(state, convId!)` calls to `flushTextForStream(state, convId)` (remove the `!`).

Also do the same for the `scheduleFlush` helper that calls `flushTextForStream(state, convId!)` — remove the `!`.

## Fix 2: Reorder `cleanupStream` vs cache write in `onDone` and `onError`

In both `sendMessage` and `editMessage`, in the `onDone` and `onError` callbacks, the cache write should happen BEFORE `cleanupStream()` to close a theoretical race window.

Current pattern (in onDone):
```typescript
cleanupStream();
if (activeConversationIdRef.current === convId) {
  setIsStreaming(false);
} else if (convId) {
  messagesCacheRef.current.set(convId, state.messages);
}
```

Change to:
```typescript
if (convId && activeConversationIdRef.current !== convId) {
  messagesCacheRef.current.set(convId, state.messages);
}
cleanupStream();
if (activeConversationIdRef.current === convId) {
  setIsStreaming(false);
}
```

Apply the same pattern to `onError` in both `sendMessage` and `editMessage`.

## Fix 3: Read from existing stream's messages in `editMessage`

In `editMessage`, before aborting the existing stream, save a reference to the existing stream's messages. Then use those messages (if available) instead of `messagesRef.current` for building the truncated message list.

Currently:
```typescript
// Abort existing stream for this conversation if any
if (convId) {
  const existingState = streamStatesRef.current.get(convId);
  if (existingState) {
    existingState.abortController.abort();
    // ... cleanup
  }
}
// ... later:
const currentMsgs = messagesRef.current;
```

Change to save the existing messages before abort, then use them:
```typescript
let existingMessages: ChatMessage[] | null = null;
if (convId) {
  const existingState = streamStatesRef.current.get(convId);
  if (existingState) {
    existingMessages = existingState.messages;
    existingState.abortController.abort();
    // ... cleanup
  }
}
// ... later:
const currentMsgs = existingMessages || messagesRef.current;
```

## After fixing

1. Run `cd frontend && npx tsc --noEmit` to verify zero errors
2. Commit with message: `fix: address code quality review issues in AgentContext`

Report what you changed.

